From: =?UTF-8?q?Boris=20Sta=CC=88heli?= <ich@bstaehe.li>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:33:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] User button actions: two alert levels, hold gestures,
 hint tune

- Add a second alert level (BUTTON_ACTION_SEND_ALERT2,
  BUTTON_ACTION_ACK_OR_ALERT2, alert2_text / UBA_ALERT2_TEXT, default
  "\x07SOS"). Each level has its own rate-limit window.
- Holds are handled on release again (USER_BUTTON_HOLD): a hold shorter
  than hold_alert_max_ms (UBA_HOLD_ALERT_MAX_MS) runs the single press
  action; a longer hold released before the shutdown time sends nothing
  and plays a short, friendly hint tune. A press during the tune only
  stops it. Holds reaching the shutdown time keep the stock shutdown on
  release, which avoids an immediate wake-up from a still pressed button.
- The resolver now takes the button state (nag, hint tune, time,
  per-level limiters) and the hold duration, all covered by native
  tests.
